bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    native_codegen_scope_frees_bootstrap_llvm_name_index_2026-11-09, 0, "2026-11-26 aarch64 Linux run: admitted aarch64 Stage 2 built from origin/release/1.0.0 76892f19a3a (stage2-sanity pass, sha256 567541f4ffd021a1, cranelift-built); probes built with SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP=1 SIMPLE_NATIVE_GO_TO_END=1 SIMPLE_FILE_WORKERS=0 SIMPLE_BOOTSTRAP_WHOLE_PROGRAM=1 <stage2> native-build main.spl --backend=<b> --entry-closure. Recorded repro test/s3sanity/w5_use_io_runtime.spl on --backend=llvm sent 62 modules through the LLVM codegen pool (codegen-pool ir 1..62/62), built rc=0 and printed PASS w5_use_io_runtime; 0 lines of rejected invalid array handle in build log and run output. Cranelift leg also PASS. Red side is the recorded 2026-11-09 Windows lldb trace (no pre-fix Stage 2 on this host). Status -> verified."
    native_codegen_scope_frees_bootstrap_llvm_name_index_2026-11-09, 1, "2026-11-26 correction: status back to fix-implemented-verification-pending. The aarch64 green run above has no same-host red: the only red evidence is the 2026-11-09 Windows x86_64 stage2_new4 lldb trace, and no pre-fix Stage 2 exists on this host, so the aarch64 run cannot show the fix is what removed the failure. Gap: a red on this host (a Stage 2 built from a commit before the warm-up fix, or the fix reverted) or a green re-run of the same w5 repro on Windows x86_64."
